{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IToolbarItemParams" /%}

### Providing Custom Components

A Custom Toolbar Item is set via the `toolbarItem` property of a Toolbar Item definition and can be any of the following types:

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

1. `String`: The name of a registered Toolbar Item Component, see [Registering Custom Components](./components/#registering-custom-components).
1. `Class`: Direct reference to a Toolbar Item Component.

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}

1. `String`: The name of a registered Toolbar Item Component, see [Registering Custom Components](./components/#registering-custom-components).
1. `Class`: Direct reference to a Toolbar Item Component.

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}

1. `String`: The name of a registered Toolbar Item Component, see [Registering Custom Components](./components/#registering-custom-components).

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}

1. `String`: The name of a registered Toolbar Item Component, see [Registering Custom Components](./components/#registering-custom-components).
1. `Component`: Direct reference to a Toolbar Item Component.

{% /if %}

Additional props passed to the component via `toolbarItemParams` are merged with the params defined in `IToolbarItemParams`.

